# Netlify / Cloudflare Pages SPA fallback.
#
# This is a client-side-routed app: only index.html exists on disk, and every
# other path is resolved by the router once JavaScript has run. Without this
# rule a request for /products/root-charger -- which is precisely the kind of
# URL this site is built to have shared over WhatsApp -- returns a hard 404
# from the host, because there is no such file.
#
# 200 rather than 301: the URL must stay as the visitor typed it so the router
# can read it. A redirect to / would throw away the path.
/*  /index.html  200
